  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We just re-launched the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/daily-dozen-challenge/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Daily Dozen Challenge</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to help more people discover how easy it is to fit some of the healthiest of healthy foods into their meals. Join us on </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/nutrition_facts_org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">social media</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and show us how you Do the Dozen. </span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Plan</strong>: Pick a day to eat the Daily Dozen. Download our free Daily Dozen app </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">on </span><a href=\"https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/dr-gregers-daily-dozen/id1060700802?mt=8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">iPhone</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and</span><a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=org.nutritionfacts.dailydozen&amp;hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Android</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> that features the checklist, as well as these valuable tools to help you prepare for a successful challenge: </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Evidence-Based Eating Guide</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Daily Dozen Meal Planning Guide</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and</span> <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/daily-dozen/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Daily Dozen Digest</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, our free 11-week email series.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Challenge</strong>: </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Use the Daily Dozen checklist in the app to guide you as you take the Challenge. Document your meals, snacks, and activities by taking photos and/or videos throughout your challenge day.</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Post</strong>: Share your Daily Dozen Challenge experience to inspire and motivate others. Post your Challenge pictures or videos on social media, and use the hashtag #DailyDozenChallenge to build the community of participants. </span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Encourage</strong>: The more, the merrier! Challenge others to take part in the Daily Dozen Challenge. Help spread the word!</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For inspiration on how to Do the Dozen, <span id=\"m_2179499576500011874docs-internal-guid-ea98f931-7fff-24d2-e8f0-5161ac1ef2fa\">check out these challenge videos:</span></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CnUxW0Ghqlq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.instagram.com/p/CnUxW0Ghqlq/?mc_cid%3D6faed6d8e1%26mc_eid%3DUNIQID&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1674063750938000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3nDjAzQ5ihyyIMqHfV-fM-\">Dr. Aisha Basset</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CnfacqABBPb\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.instagram.com/p/CnfacqABBPb/?mc_cid%3D6faed6d8e1%26mc_eid%3DUNIQID&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1674063750938000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2AWzYd2PzIDtPDVOCYIoR1\">Tami of Nutmeg Notebook</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4><b>Key Takeaways: Fasting </b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/fasting/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-91663\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/fasting-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"/></a> Fasting has been branded the “next big weight loss fad” but has a long history throughout various spiritual traditions, practiced by Moses, Jesus, Muhammed, and Buddha. Today, about one in seven American adults report using some sort of fasting as a means to control body weight. There are various approaches to fasting, from intermittent fasting to weeks of only water. For more on fasting, check out the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/fasting/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and videos such as </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/is-fasting-for-weight-loss-safe/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Is Fasting for Weight Loss Safe?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-benefits-of-fasting-for-healing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Benefits of Fasting for Healing</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Recipe: Corn Chowder</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/corn-chowder/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-91657\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-960x960.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-1536x1536.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-2048x2048.jpg 2048w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/corn-chowder-2-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Corn Chowder from </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet-cookbook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The How Not to Diet Cookbook</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a delicious comfort soup that’s perfect for the winter! This chowder can be as thick and creamy as you like, depending on how much of the soup you puree. Get the free recipe </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/corn-chowder/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and watch a video on how it’s made on our </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CW65KfdAtEy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>2022 Year in Review</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.app.box.com/file/1112440049522?v=year-in-review-2022\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-91669 size-medium\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-960x1306.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"221\" height=\"300\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-960x1306.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-1024x1393.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-768x1045.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-1129x1536.jpg 1129w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-1506x2048.jpg 1506w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-1200x1632.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-720x979.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc-540x734.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/yir-mc.jpg 1838w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 221px) 100vw, 221px\"/></a>Thank you for all of your support in 2022! To see what we accomplished last year, check out our 2022 Year in Review report. In addition to continuing to put out new videos and blogs each week, highlights include </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">creating </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Daily Dozen Meal Planning Guide</span></i></a><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, </span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">translating the Daily Dozen app into 14 languages, and launching the free </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/plantbased-living-series/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Plant-Based Living email series</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.app.box.com/file/1112440049522?v=year-in-review-2022\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Download the full report here</a>.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><em><b>The </b></em><b><i>Evidence-Based Eating Guide</i></b><b> in More Languages</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-91661\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/eg-mg.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"229\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/eg-mg.jpg 600w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/eg-mg-540x617.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Our popular eating guide is now available in Spanish and Chinese. You can download these versions on our new </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Guides and Handouts page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> or buy hard copies on </span><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/outreach\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">DrGreger.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b><i>How Not to Die</i></b><b> Kindle Deals</b></h4>\n<p><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-91665\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/hntd.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"201\" height=\"241\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/hntd.png 653w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2023/01/hntd-540x648.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/>How Not to Die</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is part of Amazon’s New Year, New You January Kindle deals. Kindle Unlimited subscribers can get the book through their subscription, and in the UK, it’s available for just .99p. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Top Three Videos</b></h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-90264\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Blue vitamin tablets on white surface\" width=\"213\" height=\"120\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-07-vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 213px) 100vw, 213px\"/></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/vitamin-d-may-explain-higher-bone-fracture-risk-in-vegans/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Vitamin D May Explain the Higher Bone Fracture Risk in Vegans</span></a>: <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A combination of low calcium intake and low vitamin D exposure may explain higher bone fracture rates in British vegans.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-90246\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Vitamin capsules on dark background\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/10/60-05-the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-purported-benefits-of-vitamin-k2-should-you-take-supplements/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Purported Benefits of Vitamin K2: Should You Take Supplements?</span></a>:<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Our body can make vitamin K2 from the K1 in green leafy vegetables.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-90399\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-960x540.jpg\" alt=\"Digital drawing of plaque in arteries\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/11/60-09-cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/cholesterol-and-heart-disease-why-has-there-been-so-much-controversy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cholesterol and Heart Disease: Why Has There Been So Much Controversy?</span></a>: <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Is the role of cholesterol in heart disease settled beyond a reasonable doubt?</span></p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4><b>Live Q&amp;A</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-68737\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-960x960.jpg\" alt=\"image of dr greger\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every month, I do a live Q&amp;A right from my treadmill, and the next one is January 26! </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At 3 pm ET, tune in on our </span><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Facebook</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> page, </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">YouTube</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> channel, or directly on </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NutritionFacts.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can find links to past live Q&amp;As </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on NutritionFacts.org. And check out my recent conversation on Physicians Committee for Responsible Medicine’s </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FBwlFVCboPE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Exam Room podcast</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>"
